    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0121",
      "sequence": 133,
      "meaning": "Śiva asks Girijā to hear Hari’s beautiful, vast and pure deeds sung by Vedas and Āgamas. The precise cause of Hari’s incarnation cannot be stated definitively. Rāma is beyond argument, intellect, mind and speech—this is Śiva’s view. Yet he will tell his fair-faced listener as saints, sages, Vedas and Purāṇas explain according to their understanding, to the extent he can grasp the cause. Whenever dharma declines and vile, arrogant demons increase, committing indescribable injustice while Brahmins, cows, gods and earth suffer, the compassionate Lord assumes varied bodies and removes the virtuous people’s pain. Killing demons, reestablishing gods, preserving his Vedic boundary and spreading pure glory through the world are causes of Rāma’s birth.",
