    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0123",
      "sequence": 135,
      "meaning": "When Bhagavān killed them they were not liberated, because the Brahmins’ word prescribed three births. Once, for their sake, the devotee-loving Lord assumed a body. In one cycle Kaśyapa and Aditi were his parents; in another, the renowned Daśaratha and Kausalyā. In one kalpa he incarnated thus and sanctified the world through his deeds. In another, the gods suffered after all lost battle against Jalandhara. Śambhu waged immense war, yet the exceedingly powerful demon could not be killed because his wife was supremely faithful; strengthened by her fidelity, Tripurāri could not defeat him. The Lord used a ruse to break her vow and accomplish the gods’ purpose. When she learned the secret, she angrily cursed him.",
